  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 200 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nSaturday will be the warmest day of the extended forecast as ridging \nmoves overhead for the day before shifting to the east on Sunday and \ninto the early part of next week. If Saturday's forecast high of \n102F occurs, this would be a record for the date (currently 101F set \nin 1930). Daytime highs will fall from the low 100s for most into \nthe low to mid 90s from Monday through Wednesday. Rain chances will \ngradually increase during this time, but remain confined to the \nwestern half of the CWA and top out between 10-30%. Overnight lows \nfor many will gradually dip into the 60s to low 70s for most, but \ntemperatures will still remain above normal through the middle of \nSeptember. \n\n-Stickney",
